Feature: Governed enterprise consulting skill consumption
  Mesh agents consume released consulting mechanics without gaining new authority.

  Scenario: Chief of Staff uses falsification-first PPMD method
    Given Chief of Staff already has the mesh-ppmd-bot Skill binding
    When a material explanatory decision is prepared
    Then the method may use a falsifiable Day-1 hypothesis
    And issue-tree decomposition remains distinct from hypothesis-tree testing
    And load-bearing branches include confidence, disconfirming tests, kill criteria, information-value sequencing, and reversal conditions
    And method output does not become canonical functional truth

  Scenario: CRO consumes evidence-bound stakeholder intelligence
    Given Revenue Intelligence is canonical for commercial and buying-group evidence
    When the CRO uses stakeholder or coalition information
    Then unsupported power, stance, interest, dependency, budget authority, or intent remains unknown
    And title or social activity does not prove decision power or purchase intent
    And Buyer Psychology cannot overwrite Revenue Intelligence truth

  Scenario: Executive synthesis remains decision-linked
    Given an authorized consulting workflow returns multiple findings
    When an agent prepares executive synthesis
    Then no more than three primary decision-relevant insights are used by default
    And each insight is a claim linked to evidence
    And each insight includes so-what and decision implication
    And contradictions, uncertainty, and next tests are preserved

  Scenario: Decision memo does not create authority
    Given an executive decision memo is generated
    When CoS, CRO, CFO, COO, CMO, or Answer Desk consumes it
    Then the memo preserves evidence and approval state
    And the memo does not authorize pricing, staffing, publication, external communication, or other consequential action
    And L4 and L5 approval boundaries remain unchanged

  Scenario: Outcome-first meeting preparation remains bounded
    Given an executive meeting needs preparation
    When the relevant owner contributes meeting inputs
    Then one desired outcome, pre-read, time-boxed agenda, objections, decision time, owner, next commitment, evidence gaps, and approval dependencies are explicit
    And the meeting plan does not create a commitment that exceeds delegated authority

  Scenario: Artifact-first workshop preserves delivery authority
    Given a CoS-led or PPMD-led workshop is prepared
    When COO contributes delivery evidence
    Then locked and open decisions, pre-read, breakout outputs, workstream owners, parked issues, commitments, and the decision record are explicit
    And stale availability does not become current
    And staffing or delivery commitments still require the existing approval path

  Scenario: Answer Desk does not promote drafts into policy
    Given Answer Desk receives a hypothesis, draft synthesis, decision memo, workshop artifact, or critic result
    When approval or evidence is incomplete
    Then it does not treat the artifact as established policy or precedent
    And it blocks or routes according to existing permissions and authority

  Scenario: Critic readiness does not replace design authority
    Given a Mesh executive artifact receives Green, Yellow, or Red critic findings
    When CMO or another agent consumes the findings
    Then the findings remain quality-control inputs
    And Mesh Design System and Mesh Artifact Designer retain design authority
    And publication approval remains human-gated

  Scenario: Skill capability is not agent authority
    Given the enterprise consulting Skills have expanded capability
    When any of the ten agents invokes or consumes them
    Then the registered agent count remains ten
    And canonical parentage remains unchanged
    And TaskLedger ownership remains unchanged
    And completion remains distinct from verification
    And no autonomous communication is introduced
